        "sheet-wane-dpr1-shift0.37.png",
        "sheet-wane-dpr2-shift0.png",
        "sheet-wane-dpr2-shift0.37.png"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "V3",
      "finding": "Large mare/albedo patterns, overall grey/brown material and orientation match within every displayed pair. Compact shading is not pixel-identical: fine terminator/limb and terrain-detail differences are visible, particularly at DPR2 half and gibbous phases. The retained maximum channel difference is 68; it is not erased by the low aggregate error. No obvious gross material substitution was observed.",
      "evidence": [
        "sheet-wax-dpr2-shift0.37.png",
        "sheet-wane-dpr2-shift0.png",
        "sheet-wane-dpr2-shift0.37.png"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "V4",
      "finding": "No missing disc, large coverage hole or silhouette swap is visible in the contact sheets. All forty individual initial/full alpha arrays are exactly equal. Some raw PNG pixels carry nonzero RGB with zero alpha; the sampled far-exterior pixels have alpha zero and the contact-sheet composite does not show these as visible material. This does not demonstrate stars being occluded in a native scene.",
      "evidence": [
        "wax-0.92-dpr2-0.37-initial.png",
        "wane-0.92-dpr2-0-initial.png",
        "wane-0.5-dpr2-0.37-initial.png"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "V5",
      "finding": "The gibbous dark limb is very dark in both isolated physical projections, and fine edge variation remains. These raw physical-field projections bypass calendarLinear and the final display caller. They cannot pass or fail the final approved H1 calendar appearance, night Moon opacity against stars, or ordinary native presentation on their own.",
      "evidence": [
